feat(web): Kinescope as a video activity source

The video activity offers Upload and YouTube only. A Kinescope video can be
iframed through an Embed activity, but then LearnHouse records no progress:
no video_progress milestones, no completion, no timestamped notes.

Add Kinescope next to Upload and YouTube in the create dialog. The activity is
stored as an external video with type "kinescope" (accepted by the API), and
the player is chosen by link, so an activity edited from a YouTube to a
Kinescope URL plays correctly. KinescopePlayer (new) drives Kinescope's IFrame
Player API (player.kinescope.io/latest/iframe.player.js, loaded on demand) the
way the YouTube branch drives react-youtube: progress milestones and completion
through useVideoProgress, the notes clock through registerVideoClock, and the
activity's start/end, autoplay and mute settings. The edit dialog labels a
Kinescope link as such. New strings are translated in every locale.

Covered by `kinescope.test.mjs` (which links play in the Kinescope player and
which URL the player API is given); the dialogs keep passing
`activity-create-modals.test.mjs`.
